{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1793538233,"nonce":"t67fKnSLXl5YGuhb+qqLP0/Y/NE=","message":"Levers for the remaining losers, measured on the NUC at 1d85e92c (x86_64, --fast, ZYPY_LLVM=1; PyPy 7.3.20 and CPython 3.13 local).\n\nscimark_sor (271 vs PyPy 203 ms; CI 340 vs 279). Steady state is level (38.3 vs 39.3 us per cycle); the loss is the ~97 ms the loop runs as Cranelift code. Per grid cell the Cranelift loop retires 194 instructions against LLVM's 103 (IPC 6.7 vs 5.9, so instruction count, not stalls). Why: G is eval'd, so every one of the six G[x, y] accesses per cell first tests G's class (`brcond %v77`, loop-invariant), and the Array2D path then runs `0 \u003c= x \u003c width and 0 \u003c= y \u003c height` as four compares in short-circuit diamonds before the real bounds check and load. Levers: (1) unswitch the loop on the invariant class test, which also lets bounds_version fold the _idx compares in the Array2D copy (both tiers; the Cranelift loop should approach LLVM's count and LLVM's should drop); (2) promotion policy: ZYNTAX_OPTIMIZE_QUIET_MS=0 with ZYNTAX_DISABLE_CALLEES_FIRST=1 gives 270 -\u003e 255 ms (5 runs), a cheaper LLVM pipeline does not (O2 0.28 s, O1 0.32 s vs O3 0.27 s). See 2326c5c.\n\nraytrace-simple (11.1 vs ~8.5 ms; CI ~18.5 est. vs 17.4). The LLVM code is fast enough: steady state with LLVM 7.6 ms over 40 iterations, Cranelift-only 13.6 ms; the first five iterations run 10.6 to 11.1 ms because the hot methods' LLVM versions arrive late. ZYNTAX_OPTIMIZE_QUIET_MS=0 alone: first-five mean -8%; promoting callers first makes it worse (+25%). Levers: (1) order promotions so the hot methods' installs land in the second iteration (98b90bc; if they did, the 5-iteration mean would be about 8.3 ms); (2) float-specialised method bodies for run-time numbers, ceiling -28% in every tier (float-literal copy of the kernel 7.8 to 8.1 ms).\n\nmeteor-contest (first iteration 100 vs 49 ms, mean 48 vs 39; CI 3% behind). Program thread in its first iteration (perf, 10 kHz): compiled kernel code 29 ms, compiler Rust 21, Cranelift 11, libc memory 13, kernel 11.6, interpreter 5.4, blocked 6.7. Compiles on the critical path (program thread and the first-call thread it waits on): library 35 to 36 ms, program 48 to 51 ms; the warm-up thread compiles another 142 to 147 ms of library code in the background. Levers: (1) library machine code (09dc35a) takes the 35 ms off the critical path and the 145 ms of CPU off CI's 4 cores: first iteration ~65 ms, enough for CI's 3%; (2) cheaper first compiles of program functions (solve 17 ms; per-header OSR layout analysis 2 ms in the window; b399633).\n\ndeltablue (CPython's 2 ms per iteration; zypy 43 to 52 + 9 to 12 + 0.5 x3). The program thread is on-CPU for its whole first iteration: compiler Rust 12 to 13.5 ms, Cranelift 10.5 to 14, interpreter ~12 (run_frame, ZyntaxValue clone and drop, register-file setup), libc memory 7, kernel 3. Interpreter alone runs deltablue at 117 ms per iteration (CPython 2 ms; meteor 17 s vs 76 ms): every interpreted call costs about 60x CPython. Turning the warm-up thread off makes the first iteration 143 ms; lower or higher baseline thresholds make it worse. Levers: library machine code (09dc35a; deltablue compiles 65 library functions), a faster tier 0, cheaper Cranelift compiles of small methods (0.2 to 1.1 ms each for loop-free bodies already optimised). Even all three leave a 5-iteration mean well above 2.3 ms: under --fast this kernel needs its first iteration under ~7 ms.\n\nscimark_lu (won on CI, loses 148 vs 138 on the NUC). Steady state is ahead (0.37 vs 0.55 ms per cycle at 800 cycles); at the suite's 200 cycles Cranelift alone is faster than with the LLVM tier (131 vs 153 ms), so tier-up costs it in a short run.\n\nSmall, not CI levers: glibc's per-thread arenas grow by mprotect (5500 of meteor's 6560 mprotect calls) and malloc_trim(0) after compiles makes 528 madvise calls; a no-op malloc_trim gives deltablue's first iteration 47.8 -\u003e 42.7 ms but the 5-iteration mean -1%, meteor -2%, at +5 to 7 MB anonymous memory. arena_max=4 is slower.","files":null}]}